data: {"type":"TOOL_CALL_RESULT","toolCallId":"call_01_6Z7CsKXCftJNnl4DlYNK6468","messageId":"9c9239b6-d50a-435d-80be-89816479b017","content":"{\"ok\":true,\"result\":{\"path\":\"/skills/app-ui-model/SKILL.md\",\"content\":\"1: ---\\n2: name: app-ui-model\\n3: description: Load for low-level AppUIModel composition changes, including custom add, remove, hide, move, resize, placement, Layout, or nested Plugin Slot changes. The Host-owned insert_plugin_default semantic fast path does not require this Skill.\\n4: compatibility: Agent UI Plugin Creator authoring model.\\n5: allowed-tools: enable_creator_tools read_file ls glob grep inspect_ui_project inspect_app_ui_model inspect_ui_slots list_ui_plugins inspect_ui_plugin inspect_agent_ui_sources mutate_app_ui_model purge_ui_plugin ask_user_question\\n6: ---\\n7: \\n8: # AppUIModel Composition Manual\\n9: \\n10: Use this Skill for low-level Composition changes, not for the Host-owned\\n11: `insert_plugin_default` fast path. The semantic operation already carries the\\n12: complete desired insertion and the Host deterministically resolves its\\n13: authoring-default placement.\\n14: AppUIModel owns which Plugin instances exist, whether they are enabled, their\\n15: placement, child Slot topology, and the Layout tree that contains visual\\n16: regions. Product content, presentation copy, Runtime configuration, and Plugin\\n17: behavior belong to application/source or Runtime layers.\\n18: \\n19: Always reason in this order:\\n20: \\n21: ```text\\n22: user request\\n23: -> authoritative current composition\\n24: -> desired final composition\\n25: -> semantic delta\\n26: -> one atomic mutation when the delta is determinable\\n27: ```\\n28: \\n29: Do not choose a tool operation from the wording alone.\\n30: \\n31: ## Ownership boundary\\n32: \\n33: - Composition owns AppUIModel plugin presence, enabled state, identity,\\n34:   placement, child Slot topology, Layout, Panels, Rows, Columns, Stacks, Slots,\\n35:   and Slot occupants.\\n36: - Plugin Behavior owns `/plugins/**` rendering, interaction, and child Slot\\n37:   declarations.\\n38: - Runtime Capability owns Services, Runtime stores, shared state, and Runtime\\n39:   actions.\\n40: - Agent Integration owns AG-UI, Frontend Tools, Application Events, and Agent\\n41:   contracts.\\n42: - A failure in Composition does not authorize Plugin, Runtime, or Agent\\n43:   Integration edits.\\n44: - Repair only defects introduced by this run or necessarily included in the\\n45:   user's requested final state. Report unrelated workspace-integrity blockers.\\n46: \\n47: Treat `/app-ui.json` as the editable authoring source of truth. Runtime\\n48: IR, Runtime slot ids, compiler-generated Layout ids, contributions, mounts, and\\n49: SlotRegistry state are derived and must never be edited or passed to Creator\\n50: tools. Use Operator inspections for current facts and\\n51: `mutate_app_ui_model` for every Composition write; never edit AppUIModel or the\\n52: generated Registry with filesystem tools.\\n53: \\n54: For a pure Composition request, use\\n55: `inspect_ui_project({\\\"view\\\":\\\"composition\\\"})` as the authoritative current-state\\n56: read. Its fresh snapshot already contains the model hash, compact Layout refs and\\n57: sizes, Slots and occupants, current Plugin instances and placement, available\\n58: capability summaries, Active Composition, and deterministic Layout constraints.\\n59: Each capability summary also carries positive authoring semantics when declared:\\n60: user intents, visual role, typical relative placement, recommended size,\\n61: Composition ownership, and current required/optional Service readiness. The\\n62: snapshot's `hostGuarantees` lists the legality checks performed atomically by\\n63: `mutate_app_ui_model`; `postCommitVerificationRequired: true` means admission\\n64: success is not full task verification and current-revision Host/Runtime checks\\n65: remain required after the commit.\\n66: Do not follow it with `list_ui_plugins`, `inspect_app_ui_model`,\\n67: `inspect_ui_slots`, manifest/source/CSS reads, Service inspection, or generated\\n68: file reads merely to reconfirm those facts. If a fully covered read returns\\n69: `OBSERVATION_ALREADY_COVERED`, reuse the snapshot and converge to the mutation.\\n70: Do not preflight a Host-guaranteed admission check. A summary with\\n71: `requiredServices.status: \\\"resolved\\\"` is authoritative for the current\\n72: Composition revision; it does not need a separate Service scan.\\n73: \\n74: ## Authoring invariants\\n75: \\n76: - Read visual composition from `root` downward. Layout nodes are structural;\\n77:   Layout Slots contain ordered Plugin arrays.\\n78: - A Plugin node contains only persistent `id`, `pluginId`, `enabled`, and\\n79:   optional child `slots` keyed by local Slot name.\\n80: - Plugin instance ids are persistent. Inspection `nodeRef` and `slotRef` values\\n81:   are snapshot-scoped authoring references.\\n82: - Array order is display order; do not create a separate contribution order.\\n83: - Row or Column `sizes`, when present, has one entry per child.\\n84: - Adding another visual Plugin to a Layout Slot does not enlarge its containing\\n85:   track. Check the parent track size and existing occupants: a fixed header sized\\n86:   for one control can clip or overlap them after insertion. Use separate Layout\\n87:   Slots in a Row/Column or adjust the containing track to fit the requested\\n88:   composition. Preserve the existing controls' visible content and verify their\\n89:   actual bounds; enablement and a successful transaction do not prove visibility.\\n90: - Creator Row/Column track sizes always use explicit CSS strings such as\\n91:   `\\\"280px\\\"`, `\\\"1fr\\\"`, or `\\\"minmax(0, 1fr)\\\"`. Never send numeric Row/Column\\n92:   track sizes through Creator mutation operations: Runtime numeric Row/Column\\n93:   sizes represent fractional tracks, not pixels. Existing persisted numeric\\n94:   sizes remain compatible and are not migrated.\\n95: - Inserting into a Row or Column that already has `sizes` requires the new\\n96:   child's `size` in that same insert or move operation. For\\n97:   `insert_layout_relative`, include `size` when the matching parent is sized;\\n98:   when the operation creates a new sized wrapper, provide `size` and\\n99:   `anchorSize` together.\\n100: - Stack `activeIndex`, when present, is a valid child index.\\n101: - Panel `minWidth` must not exceed `maxWidth`.\\n102: - A Plugin child Slot must be declared by its manifest and obey cardinality.\\n103:   The declaration is Parent Plugin capability; its occupants are Composition.\\n104: - A child Slot with `mode: \\\"renderer\\\"` accepts one Plugin that renders the\\n105:   current runtime entity through local scoped context. Change its occupant in\\n106:   AppUIModel to change presentation. An empty Renderer Slot renders nothing;\\n107:   disabling or removing its occupant does not reveal an implicit host or\\n108:   Agent UI fallback. Omitted `mode` remains ordinary content; do not place\\n109:   a `requiresRenderScope` Plugin in a Layout or content Slot.\\n110: - Layout Slot nodes do not gain descriptions, hints, roles, or accepts lists.\\n111: \\n112: ## Semantic operations\\n113: \\n114: - `insert_plugin_default`: insert an existing unselected visual Plugin asset at\\n115:   its declared authoring-default placement. The operation accepts only the\\n116:   complete Plugin node; never add `anchorRef`, `slotRef`, `size`, `anchorSize`,\\n117:   Panel, Row, Column, or other Layout arguments. The Host fails closed when\\n118:   placement, anchor, Service readiness, or supported Layout preconditions are\\n119:   not uniquely resolved, then the low-level Layout escape hatch remains\\n120:   available.\\n121: - `insert_plugin`: insert one complete Plugin node into `application`, a\\n122:   `layout_slot(slotRef)`, or `plugin_slot(parentInstanceId, slot)`.\\n123: - `move_plugin`: relocate an existing Plugin subtree.\\n124: - Creator's Productized move path resolves this intent once, then lowers it to\\n125:   the Host-only `move_plugin_to` semantic operation. Relative destinations use\\n126:   an anchor instance and `before`/`after`; Plugin child Slot destinations use a\\n127:   parent instance and declared Slot name. Do not replace this with remove plus\\n128:   insert or expose Layout refs to the Resolver.\\n129: - `remove_plugin` / `remove_plugin_default`: Host internal Composition removal\\n130:   primitives for an explicitly requested composition instance removal.\\n131:   Permanent source removal uses `purge_ui_plugin`; unspecified or temporary\\n132:   removal uses `set_plugin_enabled(false)`.\\n133: - `replace_plugin`: replace an instance subtree in place.\\n134: - `set_plugin_enabled`: hide or restore an existing instance.\\n135: - Layout operations use snapshot-scoped refs. All refs in a transaction are\\n136:   bound to the starting snapshot. A new node may declare a transaction-only\\n137:   `$localRef` for later operations in that same transaction.\\n138: \\n139: Prefer one complete transaction. The Host parses and compiles the draft,\\n140: checks composition and child Slot integrity, regenerates the static Registry,\\n141: and commits atomically only when its gates succeed.\\n142: \\n143: ## Canonical patterns\\n144: \\n145: ### Hide or permanently delete a Plugin\\n146: \\n147: - Explicit hiding or temporarily disabling: `set_plugin_enabled(false)`. Keep\\n148:   the instance, Layout, source, Source Lock and all Service Providers. Restore\\n149:   with `enabled=true`.\\n150: - Explicit permanent deletion including source: inspect the AppUIModel and\\n151:   Source inventory, then call `purge_ui_plugin(pluginId, appUIModelHash,\\n152:   sourceStateHash)`. Host computes all instances, orphan Provider cleanup,\\n153:   Source ownership and dependencies, final registry, verification and one atomic\\n154:   transaction. Never supply paths, dependencies or cleanup lists.\\n155: - Unspecified “不要了/不需要了/去掉”: disable the existing instance and retain\\n156:   its identity, placement, children and source. Clarify an uncertain target;\\n157:   permanent source deletion still requires the Host confirmation.\\n158: \\n159: ### Hide or purge a child Plugin\\n160: \\n161: Hide disables the child instance and preserves the parent Slot declaration.\\n162: Permanent deletion uses the Host purge tool and removes all instances of the\\n163: chosen pluginId. Clarify when the destructive outcome is uncertain.\\n164: \\n165: ### Reuse an optional capability\\n166: \\n167: Use the Composition Snapshot capability summaries to find an existing\\n168: unselected or disabled asset. Insert, enable, or reconfigure it before\\n169: considering new Plugin source. A Composition request to add an existing Theme\\n170: Switch is not Plugin creation.\\n171: \\n172: ### Move and resize\\n173: \\n174: Use `move_plugin` for Plugin relocation. Use Layout operations and current\\n175: snapshot refs for region moves and sizing. Include all already-known related\\n176: size adjustments in the same transaction. A fixed sidebar track should be\\n177: written explicitly, for example:\\n178: \\n179: ```text\\n180: [\\\"280px\\\", \\\"minmax(0, 1fr)\\\"]\\n181: ```\\n182: \\n183: ## Failure semantics and retry\\n184: \\n185: - `stale_state`: the observation cannot authorize another mutation. Refresh the\\n186:   minimum authoritative state and retry; this refresh is not a semantic replan.\\n187: - `operation_precondition`: the observation is still valid and no authoring\\n188:   state changed. Re-form the semantic delta from that observation and retry at\\n189:   most once.\\n190: - `workspace_integrity`: stop the current Composition task. Do not edit Plugin\\n191:   source, manifests, Services, Runtime, or Agent contracts unless that repair is\\n192:   explicitly in the user's requested final state.\\n193: - `infrastructure`: follow infrastructure recovery. Do not reinterpret it as\\n194:   permission for a different authoring layer.\\n195: \\n196: If an error reports `observationStillValid=true`, reuse the observation. If it\\n197: reports false, re-inspect before another mutation. A second semantic retry is\\n198: not allowed. Stale-state refreshes do not consume the one semantic replan.\\n199: \\n200: ## Golden examples\",\"hash\":\"24f74f7e6baadeb0e5b00098bff96330cb95ac9160edbac45ecf2df29193f12d\",\"totalLines\":430,\"nextOffset\":200}}","role":"tool"}

